Resolve the repository root with `git rev-parse --show-toplevel`. Create a precise `ChangeLog/` entry and keep unrelated worktree changes out of the commit.

Audit the intended diff for credentials, personal paths, machine names, hostnames, tailnet identifiers, IP addresses, databases, uploads, environment files, and other private data. Sanitize or exclude every finding before publishing.

Run `npm run verify`. Commit only the intended files, push a new branch to the configured `origin`, and open a new draft pull request targeting `main`. Give the pull request a precise title and description based on the actual change, tests, API/data considerations, and deployment impact.

Never deploy an open or unmerged pull request. If the pull request is not merged, stop after providing its URL and verification result.

After the pull request is merged, fast-forward local `main`, confirm the worktree is clean and exactly matches `origin/main`, then run `npm run prod:deploy` from the repository root. The deploy command owns backup, build, cutover, readiness, release recording, and rollback; do not copy source to another checkout or run a separate snapshot step.
